      "message": "chore: tighten the seeding guard, and shape the profile fixture for the analyzer\n\n`seed_issues.py` refused to seed a tracker that already held issues, but read a\nfailed count as an empty tracker, so an unauthenticated or rate-limited run\nseeded anyway. It now counts every issue state and refuses when the count\ncannot be established. `--force` still overrides.\n\n`basic_profile.json` described each repository with the field names\n`GitHubTool` returns rather than the ones `RepoAnalyzer.parse()` reads, so the\nlanguage, star and fork counts came through as defaults. The fixture now uses\nthe field names the analyzer reads.\n\nManifest entries track the tracker, and gain one entry for the README and\n`.env.example` key mismatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n(cherry picked from commit 5ca8ea5fb1c15c13eff8844c65678ce3a8c2de6d)",
