      },
      "message": "chore: sync the issues manifest with this repo's tracker\n\nThe manifest now mirrors the open issues on the tracker. It gains entries for\nthe 15 issues that were created directly on the tracker and were never in the\nfile, and it no longer carries entries for issues that are not open here. Each\nentry records the date its premise was checked against the code.\n\nAlso:\n\n- Adds the shared profile and resume fixtures under `tests/fixtures/`, which\n  `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` and `scripts/run_evals.py` both point at.\n- Stops `seed_issues.py` from seeding a tracker that already holds issues,\n  which would duplicate every entry. Pass `--force` to override.\n- Points the `seed_issues.py` usage example at this repo.\n- Names the fixture, not the parser, in the two README parser xfail reasons,\n  matching the reasons on the other fixture issues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n(cherry picked from commit bcf1ba67d6f71dea719fd1cfc71f3686d2f25570)",
